  "estimated_difficulty": "medium",
  "backtest_data_needs": "M1",
  "python_conversion_notes": "The CronexChaikin custom indicator must be reimplemented in Python. It computes: AD = ((Close-Low)-(High-Close))/(High-Low)*Volume, then applies fast EMA(3) and slow EMA(13) to AD series, takes the difference as the Chaikin oscillator, and smooths with signal MA(2). The crossover of main vs signal drives entries. SL=30 points, TP=70 points (adjust for 5-digit vs 4-digit brokers). New-bar guard means only one signal evaluation per completed bar.",
